 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T20:24+08:00",
 "answer": "**No, it is generally not safe to exercise outdoors in Jurong right now.** \n\nSingapore has been experiencing a severe haze situation driven by smoke from regional fires, with the western region (including Jurong and Taman Jurong) heavily impacted. Real-time air quality monitors and international AQI trackers show readings in the unhealthy to very unhealthy range for the area.\n\n### Health Advisory Guidelines:\n* **For Unhealthy / Very Unhealthy Air Quality:** National Environment Agency (NEA) guidelines advise the public—especially children, the elderly, and those with pre-existing heart or lung conditions—to **reduce or avoid prolonged or strenuous outdoor physical exertion**. \n* **Facility Closures:** Authorities like Sport Singapore have proactively closed outdoor and non-air-conditioned ActiveSG facilities due to the haze.\n\n### Recommendations:\n* **Move indoors:** Shift your workouts to indoor, air-conditioned spaces (like a gym or home) where air filtration can reduce pollutant exposure.\n* **Check live updates:** Check the official [NEA Haze Microsite](https://www.haze.gov.sg/) or local weather channels before heading out, as air quality conditions can fluctuate throughout the day.",
